/**
 * Offline-first service worker: the app always runs from the copy saved on
 * the device, and new versions arrive complete and verified, or not at all.
 *
 * Install: download every file of this version (FILES, generated by
 * `npm run build` with the SHA-256 of each file's content) into a cache named
 * after the version. Downloads bypass the HTTP cache, and a file that fails
 * to download or does not match its hash fails the whole install. A version
 * is therefore saved exactly and completely, or not at all, and the previous
 * one keeps running untouched.
 *
 * Fetch: cache-first. Every file of the app comes from the saved version,
 * online or offline, so launching never waits for the network (not even on a
 * weak connection) and never mixes files from two versions. Requests for
 * anything else, such as the install-dialog screenshots, go to the network.
 *
 * Updates: whenever the app is opened online (and hourly while it stays
 * open), the browser compares sw.js with the copy it has. A new version
 * downloads in the background and then waits. It takes over the next time
 * the app starts, or right away if the page asks (the "Restart to update"
 * button sends SKIP_WAITING). Activation deletes older versions of this app's
 * cache only, so other apps on the same origin (e.g. other GitHub Pages
 * projects) keep theirs.
 */

